---
title: Christmas Cake
course: Dessert
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: British
---

Double line a #20 cm cake tin{} with greaseproof paper, leaving it protruding about 2.5 cm.

Cream the @butter{225%g} and @soft brown sugar{225%g}. Mix with the @eggs{4} and half the @self-raising flour{225%g}. Add the @marmalade{1%tbsp}, @black treacle{1%tbsp}, @coffee{1%tbsp}(mixed with a little water), @ground ginger{1%tsp}, and @nutmeg{1%tsp}.

In another bowl mix the dried fruit (@raisins{225%g}, @currants{225%g}, @sultanas{225%g}, and @glacé cherries{225%g}) with the remaining flour until thoroughly covered, then mix with the other ingredients. Place in the lined cake tin.

Bake at 120°C (or preferably 125°C non-fan) for 3 to ~{3.5%hours}.

Towards the end of the cooking time cover with brown paper if the top appears to be burning.